From bf484c332733ab78301ffc79948b3da30f0f810b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:42:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin I-442: antialiased alpha-tested foliage under MSAA
 (grass, leaves, fences) - hdAlphaAA, default supersampled alpha test

- Alpha-tested "solid" draws on a multisampled pass (blend<=1, or blend 2 with depth write: ground clutter) get a key bit:
  hdAlphaAA 1 = alpha to coverage (alphaRef zeroed so alpha becomes the sample mask, blending off; capture copies keep the
  hard test for the Cata mirror and shadow cut-outs); 2 (default) = supersampled alpha test (sampleShadingEnable, min 1,
  pixel module loaded as a per-sample variant: user inputs decorated Sample, SampleRateShading added, patched at load,
  nothing retranslated); falls back to 1 without the sampleRateShading feature. 1x passes never change.
- hdAlphaAAInfo reports the mode in use; changes live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
